  "headline": "FDA's records trace our diazepam supply to a plant classified OAI 1095 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["E6", "D6"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Both Corvale sites use diazepam labeled by ASCLEMED USA INC. with NDC 76420031610, which is manufactured at FEI 3001452204.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2", "E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1067059 at that plant ended on 2018-09-27 and was classified OAI, with the classification known on 2018-12-26.",
      "cites": ["E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The shortage was posted on FDA's list on 2022-06-15, which is 1095 days after the OAI inspection end date.",
      "cites": ["D6", "E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The plant also received a Warning Letter on 2019-06-11 and had prior VAI inspections in 2013 and 2015.",
      "cites": ["E7", "E3", "E4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "As of 2026-10-21 the shortage has been on FDA's list for 52 months.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based transfer option moves 34 units from Corvale General (18 days on hand) to Corvale East (4.7 days on hand, reaching 10 days).",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Alternate manufacturers A-S Medication Solutions and Advanced Rx Pharmacy of Tennessee are not on FDA's shortage list today, but their labels name no plant we could place.",
      "cites": ["D4", "D5"]
    }
  ]
}
